WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:04.646
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.771 --> 00:08.108
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.192 --> 00:11.945
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.071 --> 00:14.155
"On which we used to rely?

00:14.780 --> 00:18.119
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.202 --> 00:23.206
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.330 --> 00:24.791
"Laugh and cry

00:24.791 --> 00:30.214
"He's a family guy

00:31.048 --> 00:35.427
"Alan Adler, David Preslack, Julie Axlerod,
Shep Sutton, Scott McCormack. "

00:35.511 --> 00:39.807
Those were the people who were mean to me
in junior high. Tomorrow, high school.

00:39.890 --> 00:43.978
Finally we go to Asian reporter
Tricia Takanawa for 60 seconds of filler.

00:44.062 --> 00:49.608
I'm here on Spooner Street where several
Quahog families are holding a car wash

00:49.691 --> 00:53.571
to raise money for an organ transplant
for young Paul Lewis.

00:53.655 --> 00:57.826
- What do you call this device, Paul?
- An iron lung. It keeps me from dying.

00:57.950 --> 01:00.120
I wanna play baseball!

01:00.245 --> 01:03.457
With me is one of Paul's
classmates, Chris Griffin,

01:03.582 --> 01:08.378
who helped organise this charity event.
You're a very thoughtful young man, Chris.

01:08.378 --> 01:10.756
- Can I say hello to my mom?
- Sure.

01:10.882 --> 01:13.592
- Hi, Mom!
- Hi, sweetheart.

01:13.676 --> 01:18.889
So you want the full wash... Oh, you've got a
nick there. I can probably get that out for you.

01:19.014 --> 01:24.103
If you want to go with a scent, I've got
PB and J, Sugar Cereal, and New Toy.

01:24.228 --> 01:26.189
What the deuce?

01:26.314 --> 01:30.778
- Hey! Somebody dropped a money clip.
- Wow! $26.

01:30.903 --> 01:34.864
- I've never seen so much money at one time.
- What should we do with it?

01:34.948 --> 01:38.826
I say we buy 26 dollars' worth
of ice cream and just pig out.

01:38.909 --> 01:42.998
We can dish, talk about who's getting fat.
We'll be great big bitches.

01:42.998 --> 01:45.501
Hold on, kids. That's not your money yet.

01:45.584 --> 01:49.047
You gotta put up signs and wait
two weeks for someone to claim it.

01:49.047 --> 01:51.131
If no one does, it's yours.

01:51.214 --> 01:53.300
Ah, lunch is here!

01:55.928 --> 01:58.013
Everyone, we've reached our goal.

01:58.097 --> 02:01.851
It looks like somebody's
gonna live to see puberty.

02:01.975 --> 02:04.895
- Oh, my God! That man took our money!
- What man?

02:04.895 --> 02:08.732
He wore a Jimmy Carter mask,
like the robber in that Keanu Reeves movie.

02:08.858 --> 02:12.402
- The Matrix?
- No. They were jumping out of a plane.

02:12.402 --> 02:14.697
- Executive Decision.
- That was Kurt Russell.

02:14.780 --> 02:17.408
The other guy in this movie
looks like Kurt Russell.

02:17.492 --> 02:21.371
- He's getting away!
- Don't worry. He won't get far.

02:22.204 --> 02:24.166
Stop! Police!

02:55.448 --> 02:57.533
- Joe, what happened?
- I got the money.

02:57.659 --> 03:00.662
- All right, Joe!
- But I lost the perp.

03:00.787 --> 03:04.207
Well, the money's the important thing.
Now Paul can get his...

03:04.333 --> 03:06.291
Point Break! That was the movie.

03:08.587 --> 03:12.257
Here's to Joe, who helped
little Paul get a new liver

03:12.340 --> 03:16.845
and, barring a massive infection,
a new lease on life.

03:16.845 --> 03:19.848
Don't you understand? I lost the perp.

03:19.973 --> 03:22.267
I lost the perp!

04:22.413 --> 04:26.084
So, um... the 26 dollars
would probably be safe in my room.

04:26.167 --> 04:32.840
Right. Probably get lost among the pin-ups
of Justin Timberlake and Tom Cruise and...

04:32.965 --> 04:37.345
Blast! Who the devil do the teenagers like?
Morgan Freeman.

04:37.428 --> 04:42.768
We can't keep it in my room cos there's
an evil monkey that lives in my closet.

04:45.060 --> 04:48.191
The sad part is, he wasn't always evil.

04:49.108 --> 04:52.445
Honey, good news! I made partner!

05:01.328 --> 05:04.873
Peter, Bonnie says Joe's really
depressed about that robbery.

05:04.873 --> 05:08.420
- Why don't you go talk to him?
- I don't know. There's a game on.

05:08.503 --> 05:12.256
Shame on you. You march over there
and cheer your old friend up.

05:12.381 --> 05:15.385
Don't listen to that sissy.
Grab a beer and watch the game.

05:15.510 --> 05:17.387
That sounds good.

05:18.013 --> 05:20.306
- Oh, my God!
- Get your fat ass over to Joe's.

05:20.390 --> 05:21.434
- Buddy...
- Move!

05:21.559 --> 05:24.476
All right. Take it easy, man. Everything's cool.

05:26.564 --> 05:31.025
- Hey, buddy.
- Close the door. I don't wanna see the light.

05:31.151 --> 05:35.947
Come on, Joe. Cheer up.
What do you say you and me go roller-ska...

05:35.947 --> 05:40.953
bike-ri... jump ro...
go lay on the grass?

05:41.037 --> 05:44.582
Peter, the other day was
the first time I've ever lost a perp.

05:44.708 --> 05:47.711
It was also the first time
I've really felt handicapped.

05:47.836 --> 05:51.256
I've made up my mind about this.
I'm quitting the force.

05:51.381 --> 05:53.883
Come on, Joe.
You don't have to quit the force.

05:53.966 --> 05:57.638
You could get a desk job. Huh?

05:57.721 --> 06:01.474
- You could be a desk.
- Forget it. I'm washed up.

06:01.599 --> 06:05.980
In local news, Quahog will soon play
proud host to the Special People's Games.

06:05.980 --> 06:11.068
If you and/or a friend are disabled and would
like to challenge yourself, sign up today.

06:11.193 --> 06:14.738
Joe, that's it! You gotta compete
in the Special People's Games.

06:14.821 --> 06:17.533
Gosh, I don't know, Peter.
You really think I can?

06:17.658 --> 06:21.620
Hey, I believed you could be a desk.
Come on! I'll even be your coach.

06:21.620 --> 06:23.998
All right. Let's do it!

06:24.124 --> 06:29.419
Coming up, our exposй on conveniently
placed news reports in television shows.

06:29.544 --> 06:32.674
- But first, Peter, look out for that skateboard.
- Agh!

06:41.307 --> 06:44.436
- Had a row with a fellow in the steam room.
- You don't say!

06:44.561 --> 06:46.855
- Gave him a cauliflower ear.
- Bully!

06:46.855 --> 06:50.276
- Come on. Two more.
- Peter, you're pushing me too hard.

06:50.401 --> 06:52.778
Trust me, Joe. I know physical fitness.

06:52.903 --> 06:55.613
I was in Richard Simmons'
Sweatin' to Books on Tape.

06:55.697 --> 06:58.743
"The Red Sox were in town, but I didn't care,

06:58.826 --> 07:02.705
because it was Tuesday and
I was on my way to see Maury. "

07:02.789 --> 07:07.084
"He couldn't go to the bathroom by himself
any more, but his indomitable spirit... "

07:09.670 --> 07:13.131
How does he check out, Doc?
Is my boy ready to compete?

07:13.131 --> 07:16.886
Um... I don't quite know
how to tell you this, Mr Swanson.

07:16.886 --> 07:20.431
- You're paralysed from the waist down.
- I know.

07:21.349 --> 07:23.434
Oh, thank God!

07:24.394 --> 07:28.231
God, I was standing out there
for like 10 minutes!

07:28.356 --> 07:30.859
Whoo, boy! Is that a load off!

07:32.819 --> 07:36.073
Mort, Joe's gonna compete
in the Special People's Games.

07:36.073 --> 07:38.867
You got anything to give him
a little extra juice?

07:38.992 --> 07:44.623
You mean steroids? Peter, haven't you seen
what happens to those ladies on ESPN2?

07:44.623 --> 07:48.586
They get big hair faces and
their breasts become like flapjacks.

07:48.669 --> 07:53.590
- I was thinkin' more like a protein shake.
- Oh, God, I'm sorry.

07:53.590 --> 07:57.761
Aisle three next to the creams.
Oh, I don't like saying that word.

07:59.097 --> 08:01.934
We now return to "Touched by an Angel".

08:02.017 --> 08:06.312
- Where exactly did the angel touch you?
- Here.

08:06.395 --> 08:09.233
Who are ya gonna believe?
I got a freakin' halo!

08:09.316 --> 08:10.900
Sh, sh!

08:11.317 --> 08:14.320
- Bye. I'm goin' to the mall.
- What for?

08:14.445 --> 08:17.032
Don't worry. The $26 is safe.

08:17.157 --> 08:20.161
Safe, huh? The skirt's trying to pull a fast one.

08:20.286 --> 08:22.580
- Knuckles, get the handbag.
- Right, boss.

08:22.580 --> 08:24.665
Give me my purse, you psycho!

08:24.665 --> 08:28.711
Let's see. Make-up, chewing gum,
a picture of Meg in a two-piece swimsuit.

08:28.837 --> 08:32.672
Oh, God! I pray this is not my first memory.

08:32.797 --> 08:36.136
Cool it. I am not gonna put up
with this racket for two weeks.

08:36.219 --> 08:39.680
I'll hold on to the money.
I'm a neutral party, so it'll be safe.

08:39.764 --> 08:41.975
- OK.
- I suppose we can trust you.

08:42.058 --> 08:44.560
- Now, where is it?
- What the...?

08:44.686 --> 08:48.732
Very clever. Take another reach.
You forgot your change.

08:52.402 --> 08:56.240
Hello and welcome to the Quahog
Special People's Games. I'm Tom Tucker.

08:56.365 --> 09:00.411
I'm Diane Simmons. It's a great day
to be alive, Tom, able-bodied or not.

09:00.536 --> 09:04.999
It sure is. Today we'll see some of
our finest athletes struggle valiantly

09:05.124 --> 09:09.712
against God's twisted designs. You'll cheer,
you'll cry. You might get a cheap laugh.

09:09.712 --> 09:15.343
I know I will, Tom. In fact, by the end
of the day, we may all be going to hell.

09:15.426 --> 09:17.095
I'll see you there, Diane.

09:17.220 --> 09:19.722
It sounds like the opening
ceremonies have begun.

09:19.805 --> 09:22.433
There are the paraplegics,

09:22.934 --> 09:25.436
followed by the blind team.

09:26.478 --> 09:28.564
Still no sign of the deaf team.

09:32.443 --> 09:35.781
- You're gonna be late.
- Maybe they're not there.

09:35.863 --> 09:40.578
And now we turn our attention
to the lighting of the flame.

09:41.828 --> 09:43.915
And these games are under way.

09:43.998 --> 09:48.585
We begin with the 100-metre dash
for people afraid of yellow tape.

09:52.882 --> 09:55.883
It's anybody's race now, Tom.

09:56.009 --> 09:58.721
And it's Odai Mutambo of Kenya!

09:59.347 --> 10:03.308
The decathlon.
That's quite a mountain to climb, Peter.

10:03.308 --> 10:05.395
Joe, look at me. Look at me!

10:05.477 --> 10:07.772
- Do I have food in my teeth?
- No.

10:07.897 --> 10:09.441
Great. Thank God!

10:09.566 --> 10:13.403
Listen, Joe. You and I both know
you have what it takes to win this thing.

10:13.529 --> 10:15.613
So get out there and do it!

10:15.696 --> 10:20.077
That gold medal is mine,
pretty boy. You don't have a chance.

10:20.202 --> 10:22.704
- He may be right, Peter.
- Joe, he's an android.

10:22.788 --> 10:25.833
Don't let him push you around.
You can do this.

10:25.833 --> 10:27.501
Yeah. Yeah!

10:27.501 --> 10:30.627
You think you're so hot, fella?
Well, I can do this.

10:33.424 --> 10:36.885
Oh, crap.

10:36.969 --> 10:38.011
Let's do it!

10:38.136 --> 10:40.932
Now the first decathlon event,
the pole vault,

10:41.057 --> 10:44.268
where Joe Swanson
takes his starting position.

10:48.648 --> 10:51.066
- Way to go, Joe!
- Yeah!

10:51.149 --> 10:54.196
- How do you like that, buddy?
- A stinker says "what".

10:54.280 --> 10:57.532
- What?
- Ha, ha, ha, ha. You stupid bastard.

11:01.285 --> 11:06.500
Good to see your new fiscal responsibilities
haven't interfered with your reading.

11:06.584 --> 11:10.545
Ah! Dostoevsky, the mad Russian.

11:10.670 --> 11:12.548
Good stuff. Good stuff.

11:12.548 --> 11:15.884
You're not gonna get the $26,
and you're despicable for trying.

11:15.967 --> 11:18.179
What? Oh, you thought...

11:18.179 --> 11:21.098
I wasn't trying to get the $26.

11:21.181 --> 11:25.353
I thought we were just having
an innocent conversation about literature.

11:25.478 --> 11:27.146
Oh, you're silly.

11:27.229 --> 11:30.983
I love that you'd go there.
You're silly. Goodbye.

11:32.360 --> 11:34.653
We'll go to bulimic pie-eating in a moment,

11:34.736 --> 11:39.533
but first, decathlon frontrunner
Joe Swanson will attempt the long jump.

11:39.658 --> 11:44.455
- Come on, Joe. Break a wheel!
- I'm ready. Let's get it on!

11:48.710 --> 11:51.422
That'll knock him out of the lead.
Tough break.

11:51.547 --> 11:53.842
- Tough break, Tom.
- Good contribution, Diane.

11:53.925 --> 11:59.346
For Swanson to take the gold, he'll have
to win the final event, the 100-metre dash.

11:59.471 --> 12:03.225
- That's OK, Joe. You can still win this thing.
- That was pathetic.

12:03.309 --> 12:09.064
Tell your wife to come over to my place if she
wants a little boom-lacka-lacka-lacka-lacka.

12:09.064 --> 12:14.069
Boom-lacka-lacka-lacka-lacka.
Boom-lacka-lacka-lacka-lacka. Boom.

12:14.987 --> 12:17.824
- Peter, it's over.
- What are you talkin' about?

12:17.907 --> 12:21.369
If I couldn't catch a two-bit criminal,
how can I win a race?

12:21.452 --> 12:23.539
Hey, what kinda talk is that?

12:23.663 --> 12:29.502
It's un-American. Did George W Bush quit
even after losing the popular vote? No.

12:29.586 --> 12:35.133
Did he quit after losing millions of his father's
friends' money in failed oil companies? No.

12:35.216 --> 12:38.263
Did he quit after knockin' that girl up? No.

12:38.263 --> 12:41.472
Did he quit after he got that DUl? No.

12:41.599 --> 12:46.688
Did he quit after gettin' arrested for drunk and
disorderly conduct at a football game? No.

12:46.813 --> 12:50.359
I get the message, Peter.

13:12.465 --> 13:14.841
Gee, Peter, this water tastes kinda funny.

13:14.966 --> 13:21.098
Uh... You mean ha-ha Jerry Seinfeld funny, or
Elayne Boosler bless-her-she's-trying funny?

13:21.223 --> 13:23.934
- Racers, on your mark.
- Go get 'em, Joe.

13:24.017 --> 13:25.895
Get set.

13:43.747 --> 13:46.959
- Yeah!
- Joe Swanson wins the gold medal.

13:47.084 --> 13:50.629
- You did it, Joe
- We did it, Peter.

13:58.345 --> 14:01.265
Mommy, look at the ladyb... Agh!

14:29.835 --> 14:31.589
- Hey, speedy.
- Do I know you?

14:31.714 --> 14:34.091
- Jim Kaplan, sports agent. Like my car?
- Yeah.

14:34.216 --> 14:35.968
- It's yours. Like my pants?
- Sure.

14:36.093 --> 14:37.969
- You know what a merkin is?
- No.

14:38.052 --> 14:40.055
- Pubic wig. I got one. You want it?
- No.

14:40.139 --> 14:42.641
- Of course you don't. You wanna be rich?
- Yes.

14:42.766 --> 14:43.684
Sign here.

14:47.228 --> 14:49.315
What the hell...?

14:51.941 --> 14:56.405
I don't understand why he did that without
me. We were gonna do everything together.

14:56.530 --> 15:00.160
It was one cereal ad, Peter.
Besides, he won the medal.

15:00.285 --> 15:01.536
Yeah, I guess.

15:01.619 --> 15:05.498
Coming to ABC, the simple story
of a man and his chair:

15:08.209 --> 15:09.251
What is this?!

15:09.335 --> 15:11.837
Starring Tony Danza as Joe Swanson.

15:11.962 --> 15:14.341
Once a man at his physical peak,

15:14.467 --> 15:16.968
brought down by a cruel twist of fate.

15:19.053 --> 15:22.807
Whyyyyyy?

15:22.891 --> 15:27.062
- With Valerie Bertinelli as Bonnie.
- Joe, you must accept your limitations.

15:27.188 --> 15:29.982
Why don't you just ask me
to lay down and die?

15:30.107 --> 15:33.027
I can't live like this any more!

15:34.987 --> 15:36.030
That's it!

15:36.155 --> 15:40.619
- That's not how it happened. It was my idea.
- With Bea Arthur as Peter Griffin.

15:40.744 --> 15:44.371
You'll never make it, Joe.
Why don't you just give up right now?

15:44.496 --> 15:46.666
No. I've got to try.

15:46.791 --> 15:51.462
- Even if it's by myself.
- You're a fool, Joe. A fool.

15:54.591 --> 15:58.888
Friday on ABC, followed by "Dharma
and Greg", but you don't have to watch that.

15:58.888 --> 16:03.475
Joe wouldn't be famous if it wasn't for me.
How come he's gettin' all the glory?

16:03.475 --> 16:06.479
He's handicapped.
That makes his story inspirational.

16:06.604 --> 16:09.314
Handicapped... Hm...

16:10.149 --> 16:12.527
Agh! How did these get up here?

16:17.322 --> 16:19.408
What the hell is this, Brian?

16:19.534 --> 16:22.328
It's my new passport.
Why are you opening my mail?

16:22.453 --> 16:25.789
You weren't planning on going somewhere
with our $26, were you?

16:25.873 --> 16:29.335
For God's sake, I just had
the damn thing renewed.

16:29.335 --> 16:32.129
You're obviously taking us for saps,
but we're not.

16:32.255 --> 16:35.465
Fess up or I'll do to you
what I did to John Lennon.

16:35.590 --> 16:37.760
John, have you met Yoko? Yoko, John.

16:37.885 --> 16:41.848
You want your money? Fine.
I hope you all kill each other.

16:42.766 --> 16:47.146
All right, I know how to settle this.
Whoever wants the money, raise your hand.

16:47.271 --> 16:52.068
Ho-ho. You're smarter than I thought.
Give yourselves a round of applause.

16:52.151 --> 16:52.984
Damn!

16:55.070 --> 16:58.616
Honey, I'm gonna be late tonight.
I've got a hooker coming over.

16:58.742 --> 17:01.534
I know it's late notice,
but what about the pool guy?

17:01.659 --> 17:04.665
- Mr Tucker, Mr Griffin's here to see you.
- I gotta go.

17:04.790 --> 17:08.126
Mr Tucker, I have just become
handicapped like Joe Swanson.

17:08.209 --> 17:11.671
I demand commercial endorsements
and a TV movie based on me

17:11.754 --> 17:14.257
- starring Valerie Bertinernie.
- Mr Griffin...

17:14.382 --> 17:20.012
I even got the first piece you're gonna run.
Exclusive footage of my tragic accident.

17:20.304 --> 17:24.684
Oh, no! A car going too fast
to stop in time! Aieee!

17:27.103 --> 17:28.980
Agh! Agh!

17:29.064 --> 17:32.317
I'm handicapped now. Agh!

17:32.525 --> 17:38.033
Mr Griffin, you can't expect me to believe this.
That was clearly a scarecrow in your clothes.

17:38.158 --> 17:40.325
- Come on!
- And when I freeze-frame,

17:41.785 --> 17:43.245
you're driving the car.

17:43.371 --> 17:45.039
- There's your hook.
- Get out.

17:47.124 --> 17:49.210
Today we're here to honour Joe Swanson

17:49.292 --> 17:55.132
for pulling my one-eyed cat Bootsie out of
the old stovepipe of my grandmother's cabin.

17:55.257 --> 18:01.181
Joe Swanson won the Special People's
decathlon and we're here to honour him.

18:01.306 --> 18:05.352
- Backstabber.
- Peter, I'm sure Joe will acknowledge you.

18:05.477 --> 18:09.522
Don't forget our deal, Lois.
I sit through this and later tonight I get anal.

18:09.648 --> 18:12.567
No matter how neat I want the house,
you clean it.

18:12.651 --> 18:14.318
Thank you, thank you.

18:14.443 --> 18:17.240
You know, no one can win
a gold medal by himself.

18:17.365 --> 18:22.036
It takes friends. I want to acknowledge
a special friend in the audience today.

18:22.161 --> 18:24.037
My friend Peter.

18:24.120 --> 18:28.916
Peter Yarrow, of Peter, Paul and Mary.
Let's give him a hand, folks.

18:30.378 --> 18:33.214
That's nothing compared to
what this next man did.

18:33.214 --> 18:37.885
He challenged me to go that extra mile.
And that man is Mr Griffin.

18:38.011 --> 18:41.138
Comedian Eddie Griffin, get up here!

18:42.891 --> 18:47.603
Your acerbic anti-white humour was
a constant inspiration. Thank you, sir.

18:47.687 --> 18:51.440
And last but not least,
who could forget the fat guy?

18:51.566 --> 18:55.194
Chef Paul Prudhomme,
you get your Cajun ass up here!

18:55.321 --> 18:57.198
I didn't even do anything.

18:57.281 --> 19:00.533
That's it.
There's someone else he didn't thank.

19:00.533 --> 19:04.371
- Mr Steroid. That's how he won.
- That's not true.

19:04.496 --> 19:08.249
Yes, it is. I put steroids in your water bottle
before the last race.

19:10.420 --> 19:13.755
I'm sorry, everybody. I've let you all down.

19:13.881 --> 19:16.801
Yes. You suck. I rule.

19:16.801 --> 19:19.929
Who da man? Who da man? Who da man?

19:22.933 --> 19:27.020
All right. If anyone tries to lift the glass,
the bell will ring.

19:27.020 --> 19:30.773
- Well, let's all go to bed.
- Off we go, then.

20:04.559 --> 20:06.727
- Did you find the place OK?
- No problem.

20:06.853 --> 20:08.813
Hey, kids.

20:08.938 --> 20:12.358
I only had soup. I don't see why
we should split the bill evenly.

20:12.483 --> 20:16.030
Wake up! This is Mr Taylor.
He's here to claim the money clip.

20:16.030 --> 20:17.696
- Oh!
- Oh!

20:17.780 --> 20:19.991
Uuuuuuugh!

20:23.119 --> 20:27.083
Peter, go talk to him. After all,
you set out to make him feel better.

20:27.165 --> 20:29.793
- Now he's worse than ever.
- I don't know, Lois.

20:29.877 --> 20:35.508
He's probably waitin' to be interviewed
by Dan Rather or that dreadful Gene Shalit.

20:35.633 --> 20:38.760
I think those days are over now, Peter.

20:42.306 --> 20:45.101
- Hey there.
- Hi, Peter.

20:45.935 --> 20:49.605
- Listen, Joe, about this whole mess...
- Hold it, Peter.

20:52.190 --> 20:54.611
That's the car-wash thief.

21:05.663 --> 21:09.209
- Ha, ha! Tough luck, wheelie!
- Yeah. For you.

21:11.586 --> 21:17.217
I'm Joe, your waiter. Today's special
is justice, served cold with a side of jail.

21:17.342 --> 21:22.223
Order the soufflй now,
cos it takes 10 to 15 years.

21:24.643 --> 21:27.853
Peter, I really appreciate
what you did for me.

21:27.978 --> 21:31.314
- What do you mean?
- That slimy agent had me believing the hype.

21:31.398 --> 21:34.861
I forgot it was really you who got me
to believe in myself again.

21:34.945 --> 21:39.658
- By the way, I'm goin' back to the force.
- Good for you.

21:40.075 --> 21:42.160
What happened to the car-wash thief?

21:42.244 --> 21:45.163
Ironically, I severed his spine
when I landed on him.

21:45.289 --> 21:48.417
Looks like you got more competition
at next year's games.

21:48.500 --> 21:51.002
No. He's dead.

21:51.003 --> 22:52.003
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru